<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><p:cmLst xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:mv="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:mac:vml" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:c="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/chart" xmlns:dgm="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/diagram" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:pvml="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:powerpoint" xmlns:com="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/compatibility" xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" xmlns:p15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2012/main" xmlns:ahyp="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2018/hyperlinkcolor"><p:cm authorId="0" idx="1" dt="2023-01-19T07:00:18.584"><p:pos x="1615" y="737"/><p:text>EI team modified to make a more generic statement that the in-house EMR option is easiest to get approved.</p:text><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{C676402C-5697-4E1C-873F-D02D1690AC5C}"><p15:threadingInfo timeZoneBias="0"/></p:ext><p:ext uri="http://customooxmlschemas.google.com/"><go:slidesCustomData xmlns:go="http://customooxmlschemas.google.com/" commentPostId="AAAAnOBtgxA"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cm><p:cm authorId="1" idx="1" dt="2023-01-19T07:00:18.584"><p:pos x="1615" y="737"/><p:text>@nyah.neita@flywire.com I really don't see the improvement here... Generic is exactly what is confusing since &quot;EMR based solutions&quot; largely don't exist other than Epic.  This isn't being published publicly, so why not be specific to how our teams are structured?  Probably late now, but should speak to it</p:text><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{C676402C-5697-4E1C-873F-D02D1690AC5C}"><p15:threadingInfo timeZoneBias="0"><p15:parentCm authorId="0" idx="1"/></p